WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Ships carried waste plastic across oceans.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:09.410
Since 1992, China had imported a cumulative
45 per cent of the world's plastic

3
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.530
waste.

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.850
Chinese firms could use it
profitably as raw material.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.510
In 2016, China reported importing
about 8.8 million tonnes.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.230
In 2018, about 51,000 tonnes.

7
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.070
What happened, and where did the waste go?

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.070
Was it burned at sea?

9
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.230
Did exporters stop using plastic?

10
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.070
In this mission, you'll
follow the world's waste,

11
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.570
including a record 62 billion
kilograms of e-waste in 2022.

12
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.170
Then you'll weigh the circular economy,
which aims for materials that never become

13
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.430
waste, and how far the EU has got.

14
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.370
Your mission: find out what happened
to China's plastic waste imports,

15
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.190
and where the waste went.
